As a user, here is how I think I'd rank some of the alternatives:

BEST
 1    autocompression
 2    autodeletation after a specific warning
 3    autodeletation after a confirmed back up (aka migration to tape)
 4    autodeletation after a general notice with a chance of a back up
 5    autodeletation without notice, without backup
WORST

Levels 1, 2, 3 seem best because they don't rely on the user to
remember, for example, not to create files with a *.log extension.
(Face it, we users can't be trusted to remember such information).
And they don't rely on the regular back up (which aren't completely
reliable).

