[...]

The difference is that posting 13 Gig is substantially disruptive
regardless of content, whereas apparently your objection to the
material from CMU is that you find its content offensive. The
difference is that we can generally trust the authorities to determine
what is "substantially disruptive" (in a content neutral way), we can
not trust the authorities to determine what is offensive.

I'm not the first to draw this distinction. It is central to free
speech. It is part of the case law in the U.S. and an explict part of
the campus codes at my university and I believe many (most?)
universities in the U.S.

- Carl

